@startuml
' Figure 8.9 - State Machine Diagram: Evidence Lifecycle
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam backgroundColor white

state "Collected" as C
state "Submitted" as S
state "Under Analysis" as UA
state "Transferred" as T
state "Archived" as AR
state "Flagged" as F

C  : entry / create initial custody entry
C  : entry / compute SHA-256, sign
S  : entry / audit transition
UA : entry / recalculate risk score
UA : do / analysis performed by custodian
T  : entry / update current_holder
T  : entry / sign custody record
AR : entry / freeze item
AR : exit  / only on integrity failure
F  : entry / raise risk level
F  : entry / alert Lead and Admin

[*] --> C : register evidence

C  --> S  : submit\n[Admin, Lead]
C  --> T  : transfer\n[Admin, Lead, Analyst]

S  --> UA : begin analysis\n[Admin, Lead, Analyst]\n[≥ 1 custody log entry]
S  --> T  : transfer\n[Admin, Lead, Analyst]
S  --> AR : emergency archive\n[Admin only]

UA --> T  : transfer\n[Admin, Lead, Analyst]
UA --> AR : archive\n[Admin, Lead]\n[integrity verdict = Intact]

T  --> UA : resume analysis\n[Admin, Lead, Analyst]

C  --> F : integrity failure\n[Admin, Lead]
S  --> F : integrity failure\n[Admin, Lead]
UA --> F : integrity failure\n[Admin, Lead]
T  --> F : integrity failure\n[Admin, Lead]
AR --> F : integrity failure\n[Admin, Lead]

F  --> UA : issue resolved\n[Admin only]

AR --> [*] : case closed

note right of AR
  <b>The guard on this transition is the
  system's central procedural rule.</b>
  An item cannot be archived until a
  verification has returned Intact —
  guarantee G4 in its purest form.
end note

note bottom of F
  Reachable from <b>every</b> state,
  escapable from <b>one</b>, by <b>one</b> role.
  A Read-Only investigator appears in
  no guard at all, so the system offers
  such a user no transitions rather than
  transitions it would then refuse.
end note

legend left
  <b>Notation</b>
  [Role]      minimum role permitted
  [condition] precondition guard
  entry /     action on entering the state
  do /        ongoing activity
  14 transitions in total; the five
  "→ Flagged" edges share one guard.
endlegend
@enduml
